<figure class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-2 border-ink p-4 sm:p-6">
  <p class="font-bold">The wheels turn together, but only the outer rim rolls on the ground.</p>
  <svg
    class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm"
    viewBox="0 0 300 256"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="figure-title figure-desc"
  >
    <title id="figure-title">The wheels turn together, but only the outer rim rolls on the ground.</title>
    <desc id="figure-desc">
      Two concentric wheels start and end in the same relative positions. The outer
      circumference determines the distance moved. The inner wheel slides relative to an
      imaginary lower track.
    </desc>
    <path d="M10 190 H290" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
    <path
      d="M10 165 H290"
      stroke="currentColor"
      stroke-width="1.5"
      stroke-dasharray="6 5"
      opacity=".5"
    />
    <g fill="none" stroke-width="3">
      <circle cx="62" cy="140" r="50" stroke="#bd4b37" />
      <circle cx="62" cy="140" r="25" stroke="#387a91" />
      <circle cx="238" cy="140" r="50" stroke="#bd4b37" />
      <circle cx="238" cy="140" r="25" stroke="#387a91" />
    </g>
    <g fill="currentColor" font-size="16" text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="62" y="70">
        Start
      </text>
      <text x="238" y="70">
        After one turn
      </text>
      <text x="150" y="222">
        Same forward distance
      </text>
      <text x="150" y="244">
        for both rims
      </text>
    </g>
    <path d="M100 64 H170" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
    <path d="M163 58 L172 64 L163 70" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" />
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="text-base leading-normal">
    The large rim rolls without slipping on the solid ground line. The smaller rim never touches
    that ground; compared with the dashed imaginary track, it slides. Sharing the same journey
    does not mean the two circumferences are equal.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
